<InfoPage title="Privacy Policy" kicker="Privacy" description="How ClothOff AI Safe Guide handles visits, links, and personal data on this static educational website.">
  <h2>Summary</h2>
  <p>This is a static informational website. It has no user accounts, no image uploader, no prompt box, no payment flow, and no database for visitor profiles.</p>
  <h2>Information this site collects</h2>
  <p>The site itself does not set advertising cookies or request sensitive personal information. Our hosting and security provider may process standard technical request data such as IP address, browser type, requested URL, timestamps, and security signals to deliver and protect the site.</p>
  <h2>Images and AI prompts</h2>
  <p>We do not accept, process, or store visitor images or AI prompts. Do not send sensitive photos through contact channels.</p>
  <h2>External links</h2>
  <p>Articles may link to primary references or third-party websites. Their privacy practices are governed by their own policies. Review those policies before creating an account or uploading content.</p>
  <h2>Retention and requests</h2>
  <p>Because this site does not maintain visitor accounts or an upload database, there is normally no profile or image history for us to delete. A contact method for editorial corrections and privacy questions is provided on the Contact page.</p>
<h2>Optional Google Analytics</h2><p>With your permission, we use Google Analytics 4 to measure page visits, scrolling, outbound link clicks, device information, and referral sources. Analytics cookies help distinguish visits. Google may process this data on servers outside your country. We do not enable Google signals, advertising personalization, or advertising cookies.</p><p>Analytics is off until you choose Allow analytics. Choose No thanks to decline, or use Analytics preferences at the bottom of any page to withdraw permission and remove this site's accessible Google Analytics cookies. We remember your preference in local storage for up to 180 days, and honor Global Privacy Control and Do Not Track browser signals. We remove query strings and fragments from the page URL passed in our Google tag configuration and do not send chat messages, prompts, uploads, or contact-form contents.</p><p>Analytics cookies are configured to expire after 180 days, subject to renewal when used. Clearing cookies does not erase historical data already processed by Google. For information about Google's handling of analytics data, see <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's Privacy Policy</a>. You may also use the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>.</p></InfoPage>
